WEBVTT

00:00:00.842 --> 00:00:02.142
Here is how to evaluate

00:00:02.182 --> 00:00:02.832
an LLM app,

00:00:02.872 --> 00:00:03.957
in under a minute.

00:00:04.977 --> 00:00:06.131
Start with a fixed test

00:00:06.171 --> 00:00:06.558
set.

00:00:06.598 --> 00:00:07.801
Real questions, with the answers

00:00:07.841 --> 00:00:08.261
you

00:00:08.301 --> 00:00:08.864
expect.

00:00:09.809 --> 00:00:10.789
Then run the loop.

00:00:10.829 --> 00:00:11.536
Run the app.

00:00:11.576 --> 00:00:12.982
Score each answer.

00:00:13.022 --> 00:00:13.816
Fix the prompt or the

00:00:13.856 --> 00:00:14.698
retrieval.

00:00:14.738 --> 00:00:15.988
Then run it again.

00:00:16.922 --> 00:00:17.727
Score three things.

00:00:17.767 --> 00:00:18.947
Is the answer correct?

00:00:18.987 --> 00:00:20.197
Is it grounded in the

00:00:20.237 --> 00:00:20.507
sources?

00:00:20.547 --> 00:00:22.023
Does it follow the format?

00:00:23.202 --> 00:00:24.323
Then gate the release.

00:00:24.363 --> 00:00:25.161
If the score drops by

00:00:25.201 --> 00:00:27.229
two points, the release stops.

00:00:28.177 --> 00:00:29.297
So remember.

00:00:29.337 --> 00:00:29.958
A fixed test set,

00:00:29.998 --> 00:00:31.418
three scores, and a release

00:00:31.498 --> 00:00:31.931
gate.

00:00:31.971 --> 00:00:33.700
Write twenty questions today.

